{"id": "sdqa0057", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3320345669, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What is the oldest grave at Arlington National Cemetery?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0057.wav", "input_sha256": "0ca90695c445c67f6a4f7561f5aefb702e9e653bf91922080700daea38fac3cb", "input_samples": 66782, "input_s": 4.174, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.7729, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The answer depends on what you mean by “oldest”: Oldest grave on the grounds: Mary Lee Fitzhugh Custis, buried in what is now Section 13 after her death in 1853. Her husband, George Washington Parke Custis, was buried next to her in 1857. (nps.gov) , First military burial after Arlington became a cemetery: Private William Henry Christman, buried May 13, 1864, in Section 27, Grave 19. (arlingtoncemetery.mil)", "expert_answer": "The answer depends on what you mean by “oldest”:\n\n- **Oldest grave on the grounds:** **Mary Lee Fitzhugh Custis**, buried in what is now **Section 13** after her death in **1853**. Her husband, **George Washington Parke Custis**, was buried next to her in **1857**. ([nps.gov](https://www.nps.gov/arho/learn/historyculture/the-custis-graves.htm))  \n- **First military burial after Arlington became a cemetery:** **Private William Henry Christman**, buried **May 13, 1864**, in **Section 27, Grave 19**. ([arlingtoncemetery.mil](https://www.arlingtoncemetery.mil/Explore/History-of-Arlington-National-Cemetery/Section-27))", "transcript": "What is the oldest grave at Arlington National Cemetery?\n", "asr_s": 0.55, "expert_s": 7.02, "expert_input_samples": 66782, "expert_input_s": 4.174, "expert_input_sha256": "0ca90695c445c67f6a4f7561f5aefb702e9e653bf91922080700daea38fac3cb", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 6.475, "relay_synth_ms": 16082, "onset_chunk": 4, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 357, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 357, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0057_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "5fc11e41f3264e956acbd3eb465c1a913c99cc455e7dc0826ebdaff60184d9d8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 29.16}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0057_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "9b34e91d0fa14fec1c50436fe4e9252c380ee7fb24caa732df7ef64a0a827a45", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0057_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "9c695d479f39051e7cad4d8adc30a09cec28c5a22996a09b3e2253c113039ded", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.6}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.079, 1.143, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.089, 2.16, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.076, 3.136, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.068, 4.126, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 4.174, 4.241, 4.872, 0, 24000, 0], [5, 0, 5.174, 5.598, 5.967, 0, 14400, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 4.174, "last_real_feed_done": 4.241, "onset": 4.872, "gate_read_done": 4.872, "fire": 4.872, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.872, "stall_note": 4.873, "stall_first_pcm": 5.531, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.967, "expert_req": 4.873, "expert_resp": 12.441, "relay_synth_start": 12.442, "relay_first_pcm": 13.169, "relay_synth_end": 28.524, "first_any_pcm": 4.872, "first_answer_pcm": 13.169, "session_end": 29.528}, "ttfa_answer_s": 8.995, "ttfa_any_s": 0.698}
{"id": "sdqa0065", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 13321898, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "How large is Cougar Mountain Regional Wildland Park?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0065.wav", "input_sha256": "1c426ff6907d5f33d630c74cdc5b7870686b1f33a9cc90497ca8cad068bd1269", "input_samples": 116048, "input_s": 7.253, "n_real_chunks": 8, "score": 0.7157, "act": 0.9997, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Cougar Mountain Regional Wildland Park is over 3,000 acres in size. King County describes it as a 3,000+ acre park; some listings give a more specific figure of about 3,115 acres. (kingcounty.gov)", "expert_answer": "**Cougar Mountain Regional Wildland Park is over 3,000 acres** in size. King County describes it as a **3,000+ acre** park; some listings give a more specific figure of about **3,115 acres**. ([kingcounty.gov](https://kingcounty.gov/en/dept/dnrp/nature-recreation/parks-recreation/king-county-parks/parks/cougar-mountain?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "How large is Cougar Mountain Regional Wildland Park?\n", "asr_s": 0.66, "expert_s": 4.43, "expert_input_samples": 116048, "expert_input_s": 7.253, "expert_input_sha256": "1c426ff6907d5f33d630c74cdc5b7870686b1f33a9cc90497ca8cad068bd1269", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.498, "relay_synth_ms": 7785, "onset_chunk": 7, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0065_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "ec54ea51124e06a844418c8967e28d6b43b6a13175766b21691c407443502d60", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 14.0}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/