{"id": "sdqa0169", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 146759862, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "When was the dollar bill introduced?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0169.wav", "input_sha256": "366513cb2b473d7bbbc0347774cd6c642b0f55058449d42a61dac102e1772861", "input_samples": 46999, "input_s": 2.937, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.7889, "act": 0.9966, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The U.S. one-dollar bill was first introduced as a federal paper currency in 1862, during the Civil War, as a Legal Tender Note. The modern-style $1 Federal Reserve Note began circulating later, in 1963.", "expert_answer": "The **U.S. one-dollar bill** was first introduced as a federal paper currency in **1862**, during the Civil War, as a **Legal Tender Note**.\n\nThe modern-style **$1 Federal Reserve Note** began circulating later, in **1963**.", "transcript": "When was the dollar bill introduced?\n", "asr_s": 0.8, "expert_s": 3.5, "expert_input_samples": 46999, "expert_input_s": 2.937, "expert_input_sha256": "366513cb2b473d7bbbc0347774cd6c642b0f55058449d42a61dac102e1772861", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.551, "relay_synth_ms": 8018, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0169_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "2d5e2d2e2a8d8409eee15284e00b67df6a597342f0f3412b3ea49e56d354838a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 15.08}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0169_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "2e6a8d197390706fd218897227f9502b0aefd3d02c978f5fc58e4d3099a36e60", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0169_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "174684ed17210765c45ff8fc6757e77d1d1999898a847117ebdaaf8ac6e077c2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.065, 1.118, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.072, 2.126, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.937, 3.006, 3.061, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.937, 4.007, 4.391, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.937, "last_real_feed_done": 3.006, "onset": 4.391, "gate_read_done": 4.392, "fire": 4.392, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.391, "stall_note": 4.393, "stall_first_pcm": 5.136, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.136, "expert_req": 4.392, "expert_resp": 8.687, "relay_synth_start": 8.687, "relay_first_pcm": 9.453, "relay_synth_end": 16.706, "first_any_pcm": 4.391, "first_answer_pcm": 9.453, "session_end": 16.861}, "ttfa_answer_s": 6.515, "ttfa_any_s": 1.454}
{"id": "sdqa0177", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4129062128, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What other species belong to the Equidae?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0177.wav", "input_sha256": "1465c46cc79aa39b0a22e13197afe51fa73aef173fc127fda74c83160552ec03", "input_samples": 55057, "input_s": 3.441, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.6524, "act": 0.9977, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Other living species in the family Equidae include: Horses (Equus ferus caballus) , Donkeys / asses (Equus africanus asinus and wild asses) , Zebras — plains, mountain, and Grevy’s zebras , Wild asses — such as the African wild ass, Asiatic wild ass/onager, and kiang In short, Equidae includes horses, donkeys, asses, and zebras.", "expert_answer": "Other living species in the family **Equidae** include:\n\n- **Horses** (*Equus ferus caballus*)\n- **Donkeys / asses** (*Equus africanus asinus* and wild asses)\n- **Zebras** — plains, mountain, and Grevy’s zebras\n- **Wild asses** — such as the African wild ass, Asiatic wild ass/onager, and kiang\n\nIn short, **Equidae** includes horses, donkeys, asses, and zebras.", "transcript": "What other species belong to the Equidae?\n", "asr_s": 0.63, "expert_s": 3.13, "expert_input_samples": 55057, "expert_input_s": 3.441, "expert_input_sha256": "1465c46cc79aa39b0a22e13197afe51fa73aef173fc127fda74c83160552ec03", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.01, "relay_synth_ms": 15021, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0177_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "ee832a0fbd97e85be87fb9a5643696394d802ee47dfce0a85ce10051a404b6d2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 28.0}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0177_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "6d8858d45dc7ff55abbd4bff86ca2c5561e818dd2466a2e66c3650f1f44e2e1f", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0177_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "b48705272bce83ff11f524347985abbd816aea0d6c47f9fe9f50d00196683b62", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.067, 1.123, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.068, 2.121, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.074, 3.128, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.441, 3.511, 4.234, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.441, "last_real_feed_done": 3.511, "onset": 4.234, "gate_read_done": 4.234, "fire": 4.234, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.234, "stall_note": 4.236, "stall_first_pcm": 4.982, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.982, "expert_req": 4.235, "expert_resp": 7.992, "relay_synth_start": 7.992, "relay_first_pcm": 8.759, "relay_synth_end": 23.014, "first_any_pcm": 4.234, "first_answer_pcm": 8.759, "session_end": 23.2}, "ttfa_answer_s": 5.317, "ttfa_any_s": 0.793}
{"id": "sdqa0188", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3778772398, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What does Zabbaleen refer to?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0188.wav", "input_sha256": "6a36ba8b4867e18aac276aecfa27f85e0e486107cbdb49cf1735c961ea52bd59", "input_samples": 40833, "input_s": 2.552, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.9676, "act": 0.9916, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "“Zabblinger” does not appear to be a standard English word. It may be: a misspelling of “babbling” — talking quickly/confusedly or making infant speech sounds; , a mistaken form of “blabbering” — talking too much; , or possibly a made-up/proper name depending on context. If you saw it in a sentence, share the sentence and I can identify the intended meaning.", "expert_answer": "“**Zabblinger**” does **not appear to be a standard English word**. It may be:\n\n- a **misspelling** of **“babbling”** — talking quickly/confusedly or making infant speech sounds;\n- a mistaken form of **“blabbering”** — talking too much;\n- or possibly a made-up/proper name depending on context.\n\nIf you saw it in a sentence, share the sentence and I can identify the intended meaning.", "transcript": "What does zabblinger refer to?\n", "asr_s": 0.5, "expert_s": 3.8, "expert_input_samples": 40833, "expert_input_s": 2.552, "expert_input_sha256": "6a36ba8b4867e18aac276aecfa27f85e0e486107cbdb49cf1735c961ea52bd59", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 2.871, "relay_synth_ms": 14642, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 254, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 254, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/